- trilog should drop the pico target, it can stay as an interpreter and even integrate this project as its runtime
- this repo will take the pico target and sidestep dynamic compilation by running bytecode over the network on demand
- keep Scryer for compilation, trilog could compile as well but Scryer has more libraries
- TCP/IP stack on the rpi2040 running 9P
- a compiled ZIP image can be copied and loaded over 9P like: `cp program.bin /mnt/pico/image`
- a ZIP compiled bytecode validator will run throu it, checking for ZIP version and general compatibility (opcodes and board gpio capatibilties)
- each board should have a queriable gpio table in prolog, so the sender knows what programs could work
- there should be a file that you write your queries in, trilog's parse.c could be reused for this, it should be possible to run a query from a loaded image aswell
- there should be an output file where you can stream ZIP's output
